<section class="section" aria-labelledby="stages-title">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="section-head">
      <h2 id="stages-title">Who holds what, at each stage</h2>
      <p>Most sites describe a process. The questions that matter are who you speak to, who has your details, and who is responsible for each part of the work.</p>
    </header>
    <section class="data-table-wrap" tabindex="0" aria-label="Enquiry stages table, scrolls sideways on small screens">
      <table class="data-table stage-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">What happens</th><th scope="col">Who has your details</th><th scope="col">Who is responsible for the work</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">1. Call</th><td>You call and describe the work. The {% routeLink "/request-an-accountant/", "requirements page" %} shows what to have ready.</td><td>AccountOrbit ({{ site.owner.name }})</td><td>No one yet. Nothing has been agreed.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">2. Discussion</th><td>Deepak discusses the requirement with you directly, including any dates you are working to.</td><td>AccountOrbit</td><td>No one yet.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">3. Scope</th><td>The task, the records involved, the timing, and any part the law reserves for a qualified professional are clarified.</td><td>AccountOrbit</td><td>No one yet. You can stop here.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">4. Next steps</th><td>Deepak coordinates the next steps. If another professional is needed for part of the work, your details are shared with them only if you agree.</td><td>AccountOrbit, and any professional you agree to</td><td>Before work starts, get in writing who does and signs each part, and the fee.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">5. The work</th><td>The work goes ahead as agreed in writing.</td><td>As agreed with you</td><td>Whoever is named in writing for each part. You remain responsible for your own filings and records.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </section>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" aria-labelledby="not-title">
  <div class="wrap two-col">
    <div>
      <h2 id="not-title">Where the law draws lines</h2>
      <ul class="tick-list plain-list">
        <li>A statutory or tax audit report must be signed by a practising Chartered Accountant</li>
        <li>Representation before GST or income tax authorities is limited to the people each law allows</li>
        <li>Some certificates must come from the professional the rule names</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="para">AccountOrbit is not a firm of Chartered Accountants. Any reserved part of your requirement is identified when the scope is clarified, and must be done and signed by someone qualified for it. The <a href="/#who">who-does-what table</a> sets out the main cases. AccountOrbit never asks for passwords or OTPs.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h2>Questions people ask before they call</h2>
      <dl class="open-points">
        <div><dt>Fees</dt><dd>Ask Deepak about fees for your requirement on the call, and get the scope and full fee in writing before any work starts. {% pending "whether enquiries are free, and how fees are charged." %}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>If you have a deadline</dt><dd>Mention any close filing or reply date at the start of the call. If it is very close, contact a qualified professional directly as well. {% pending "who reviews enquiries and how soon." %}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>If AccountOrbit cannot take it on</dt><dd>Some requirements may not be work AccountOrbit can coordinate. We will not suggest anyone unsuitable just to close an enquiry. {% pending "how and when you are told." %}</dd></div>
        <div><dt>Checking credentials</dt><dd>We do not label anyone verified or screened. Check a CA's membership on {% ext "https://caconnect.icai.org/search-your-ca", "ICAI CA Connect" %} and any other qualification with the body that issued it.</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

